{"engine_version":"0.29.3","file":"meo-leo-fused-pvt.toml","toml":"# Fused MEO and LEO pseudorange positioning: GPS and Galileo with a LEO navigation layer.\n#\n# A receiver in Madrid tracks the GPS baseline constellation (GPS SPS Performance Standard,\n# 5th edition), Galileo (Walker 24/3/1, Galileo OS SDD) and a LEO navigation constellation\n# (the public Xona Pulsar X5 signal: 10.23 Mchip/s in the L5 band, received power -144.9 to\n# -136.2 dBW, arXiv:2509.19551). Each system carries its own receiver clock, so the\n# inter-system bias of Galileo and of the LEO layer is estimated with the position; the LEO\n# pseudoranges are simulated with a 40 ns bias to show it recovered. Every pseudorange's\n# sigma is the delay-lock-loop thermal noise at the C/N0 of its elevation combined with the\n# system's signal-in-space range error.\n#\n# The report compares GNSS-only, LEO-only and fused fixes epoch by epoch and gives the PDOP,\n# HDOP and VDOP against the number of LEO satellites added to the GNSS geometry (highest\n# elevation first). MODELLED.\nkind = \"leo-pvt\"\nmode = \"joint\"\nseed = 3\nduration_s = 1800.0\nstep_s = 30.0\n\n[user]\nlat_deg = 40.42\nlon_deg = -3.70\nheight_m = 650.0\n\n[joint]\nmax_leo_sweep = 12\n\n[[system]]\nname = \"GPS\"\npreset = \"gps-baseline\"\ncn0_dbhz = [38.0, 48.0]\nsisre_m = 0.6\n\n[[system]]\nname = \"Galileo\"\npreset = \"galileo\"\ncn0_dbhz = [38.0, 48.0]\nsisre_m = 0.3\nisb_ns = 12.0\n\n[[system]]\nname = \"Pulsar X5\"\nleo_preset = \"xona-pulsar\"\nsignal = \"X5\"\nisb_ns = 40.0\n","summary":"LEO PVT (joint) at 40.42, -3.70 over 1800 s\n  GPS          gnss    24 sats at  20182 km, 1575.42 MHz\n  Galileo      gnss    24 sats at  23222 km, 1575.42 MHz\n  Pulsar X5    leo    258 sats at   1080 km, 1190.52 MHz\n  LEO ranging satellite in view on 100.0% of epochs\n  GNSS only  availability 1.000, median PDOP 1.47, RMS 3D error 1.06 m\n  LEO only   availability 1.000, median PDOP 1.73, RMS 3D error 0.49 m\n  fused      availability 1.0